# Harness discipline

Enforced in agent workflow, not only CI. See `.cursor/rules/harness-artifacts.mdc` for paths.

## Always

- **GitHub issue** for every change (including S).
- **plan → generate → review** — lighten artefacts for S, never skip the loop.
- Update **`docs/project/generator-state.md`** when implementation state changes.
- Update **`docs/project/roadmap.md`** when an issue closes.
- **`CHANGELOG.md`** entry for every S issue; user-facing M+ recommended.

## Feedback layout

One folder per issue: `docs/project/feedback/<n>/`

Filenames: `<reviewer-type>-i<iteration>.md`, `generator-response-i<iteration>.md`

Reviewers **own** their files; generator **only** writes `generator-response-i*.md`.

Prior iteration files are **immutable** — add new files for the next round.

## Generator must not author

- `code-review-i*.md`, `api-review-i*.md`, `security-review-i*.md`, `frontend-eval-i*.md`, `mcp-review-i*.md`, `database-review-i*.md`, `performance-eval-i*.md`, `docs-review-i*.md`

## Reviewers must not

- Implement fixes in the same pass as review
- Edit generator-owned `generator-response-i*.md`
- Mutate a previous iteration's review file

## ADRs

- **accepted** ADRs are binding; **proposed** are not.
- Generator stops if implementation needs a fork not covered by an accepted ADR → invoke `architect`, wait for human acceptance.
- Architectural PR changes need linked ADR (`code-reviewer` flags gaps).

## Lifecycle

Check `docs/project/project.md` → **Lifecycle stage** (MVP / Live / Mature) before large refactors. See `.cursor/rules/lifecycle-change.mdc`.

## Exceptions

`skip-harness-check` in PR body + reason — rare, human-approved only.